# Line endings
# The repository stores every text file with LF, and every checkout gets LF too, whatever core.autocrlf or core.eol
# say. The build must not depend on the checkout: the deterministic PDB checksums each source file and embedded
# resource, and the DLL embeds the PDB's id, so a CRLF checkout of the same commit produced a different
# SkylineTogether.dll and build id than an LF one (docs/dev/building.md#reproducible-builds).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF on every platform, or bash fails on the carriage returns.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows scripts are always checked out with CRLF (cmd.exe and Windows PowerShell 5.1 expect it).
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Solution files: Visual Studio rewrites them with CRLF.
*.sln text eol=crlf

# Binary content
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.zip binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.dmp binary
